{
  "id": "ticket_01KY93E3CBDVRBMPNNAHH4Q2FN",
  "name": "CLI input validation: reject truncated numerics, fix actor-fail exit code, bound --port",
  "slug": "cli-input-validation-reject-truncated-numerics-fix-actor-fai",
  "spec": {
    "summary": "parseIntegerOption/parseBudgetFlag use parseInt and silently truncate leading-numeric garbage (--priority 2abc -> 2, --priority 1.9 -> 1, --budget 100abc -> 100), violating the exit-2 contract and (for priority) persisting a different value than typed. Actor-resolution failure exits GENERIC_ERROR(1) not USAGE_ERROR(2). --port accepts out-of-range values (99999, -1).",
    "details_md": "",
    "acceptance": [
      "Numeric option parsers reject any value whose full trimmed string is not an integer (return USAGE_ERROR exit 2), in shared.ts parseIntegerOption and context.ts parseBudgetFlag",
      "Actor-resolution failure throws SlopError with EXIT_CODES.USAGE_ERROR",
      "--port is bound-checked to 0-65535 (0 keeps its pick-a-free-port meaning)"
    ],
    "context": [
      "src/cli/commands/shared.ts:37-45 parseIntegerOption",
      "src/cli/commands/context.ts:25-34 parseBudgetFlag",
      "src/cli/actor.ts:171-176 (missing exit code arg)",
      "src/cli/commands/web.ts:53-58 --port"
    ],
    "meta": {},
    "v": 1
  },
  "state": "done",
  "priority": 2,
